entries[91757] = { ["name"] = "Tyrande's Favorite Doll", ["text"] = "2 sec cast 15\nTyrande Whisperwind is the high priestess of Elune, and with her recent marriage, she is no longer sole ruler of the night elves. She grew up in the ancient city of Suramar, far from the first Well of Eternity, not far from the brothers Malfurion and Illidan Stormrage. Tyrande's idyllic childhood proved to be in sharp contrast to the sorrow and conflict that she would endure later in her life.\nTyrande's Favorite Doll\nBinds to account\nUnique-EquippedTrinket\n+321 Intellect\n85\nEquip: Recaptures 20% of the base mana cost of your spells, and stores it within the doll to be released at a later time. Up to a maximum of 4200 mana can be stored.\nUse: Releases all mana stored within the doll, causing you to gain that much mana, and all enemies within 15 yards take 1 point of Arcane damage for each point of mana released. (1 Min Cooldown)" }
entries[91758] = { ["name"] = "Signal Flare Camo" }
entries[91759] = { ["name"] = "Skyshredder Explosion" }
entries[91760] = { ["name"] = "Endure the Transformation", ["text"] = "Instant\nEndure the transformation for 20 sec." }
entries[91761] = { ["name"] = "Bones of Transformation", ["text"] = "2 sec cast 15\nWhen the first Well of Eternity imploded, it sank the center of kaldorei culture to the bottom of the sea. To escape certain doom, Queen Azshara made a pact with a greater power, possibly an Old God or an elemental. As a result, a curse descended upon the surviving Highborne, who became twisted, serpent-like creatures now known as the naga.\nBones of Transformation\nBinds when picked up\nToy\nUse: Endure the transformation for 20 sec. (10 Min Cooldown)" }
entries[91762] = { ["name"] = "Carcanet of the Hundred Magi", ["text"] = "2 sec cast 5\nDuring the Troll Wars, the elves of Quel'Thalas were nearly defeated by the Amani trolls. In desperation, the elves taught the humans of Arathor the ways of arcane magic. The elves taught only one hundred humans, the bare minimum needed to defeat the trolls. The humans proved to be clumsy spellcasters but had a natural affinity for magic.\nCarcanet of the Hundred Magi\nBinds when picked up" }
